<title>USA: Worldtex sees 1997 results outpacing 1996.</title>
<headline>Worldtex sees 1997 results outpacing 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HICKORY, N.C. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Worldtex Inc said on Thursday it expected better results in 1997 compared to 1996, with net sales of about $229 million and net income of about $13.2 million, or $0.90 per share.</p>
<p>For 1996, Worldtex said it projected net sales would be about $208 million and net income would be about $11 million, or $0.75 per share.</p>
<p>The company said its forecasts were based on continued favorable economic conditions and expected trends in Worldtex markets. The company also said it could not guarantee its actual results would be the same as these projections.</p>
<p>Worldtex supplies customers with covered elastic yarn.</p>
</text>
